<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duke Huan of Zheng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 771 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Duke Huan of Zheng was a younger brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-xuan-of-zhou">King Xuan of Zhou</a>, who enfeoffed him with Zheng in the Wei valley in 806 BCE. Foreseeing the collapse of the Western Zhou, he moved his family and wealth east towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a>. He served as minister of the royal court and was killed with King You when the capital fell in 771 BCE.</p></div>
